ARTICLE = '<!doctype html><html lang="en-US"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Hostinger VPS pricing: prepaid totals and renewal cash flow | VPS Cost Lens</title><meta name="description" content="Official Hostinger VPS promotional and renewal prices, prepaid totals, included weekly backups and a clearly labelled renewal cash-flow estimate."><link rel="canonical" href="https://vpscostlens.com/pricing/hostinger-vps/"><link rel="stylesheet" href="./page.css"></head><body><header><a href="/">VPS Cost Lens</a><span>Official-source price index</span></header><main><h1>hostinger vps pricing</h1><p>KVM 1 is <strong>$6.49/month promotional equivalent</strong> for a <strong>24-month prepaid term</strong>, with <strong>$155.76 payable upfront</strong> and a published <strong>$11.99/month renewal equivalent for the same term</strong> [H1]. These are the public card amounts before VAT, not a personalized checkout quote.</p><h2>Promotional, regular and renewal prices</h2><p>USD, as displayed on the public Black Friday VPS page. Promotional equivalents apply to the initial term; renewal equivalents are separate. The regular-reference column identifies the observed 1-month-term renewal rate: each amount matches the crossed-out reference shown in the official VPS purchase flow with Period set to 1 month. The 1-month introductory payment is a different price. To reproduce R1–R4, open the official VPS page, choose the named plan, and set Period to 1 month. Reference-column verification: 2026-11-12 13:51 UTC. The available Period options were 1, 12 and 24 months; a 48-month option was not offered.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><tr><th scope="col">Plan</th><th scope="col">Promotional monthly equivalent</th><th scope="col">Regular reference: 1-month-term renewal</th><th scope="col">Renewal monthly equivalent</th><th scope="col">Initial term</th><th scope="col">Payable upfront</th></tr><tr><td>KVM 1</td><td>$6.49/mo · promotional [H1, price line]</td><td>$19.49/mo · observed renewal with Period = 1 month [R1]</td><td>$11.99/mo · renewal [H1, renewal sentence]</td><td>24 months [H1, payment sentence]</td><td>$155.76 · first-term payment [H1, payment sentence]</td></tr><tr><td>KVM 2</td><td>$8.79/mo · promotional [H2, price line]</td><td>$24.49/mo · observed renewal with Period = 1 month [R2]</td><td>$14.99/mo · renewal [H2, renewal sentence]</td><td>24 months [H2, payment sentence]</td><td>$210.96 · first-term payment [H2, payment sentence]</td></tr><tr><td>KVM 4</td><td>$12.99/mo · promotional [H3, price line]</td><td>$42.99/mo · observed renewal with Period = 1 month [R3]</td><td>$28.99/mo · renewal [H3, renewal sentence]</td><td>24 months [H3, payment sentence]</td><td>$311.76 · first-term payment [H3, payment sentence]</td></tr><tr><td>KVM 8</td><td>$25.99/mo · promotional [H4, price line]</td><td>$73.99/mo · observed renewal with Period = 1 month [R4]</td><td>$49.99/mo · renewal [H4, renewal sentence]</td><td>24 months [H4, payment sentence]</td><td>$623.76 · first-term payment [H4, payment sentence]</td></tr></table></div><p class="source-note">Data source: official Hostinger pages · 2026-11-12 12:05 UTC · <a href="https://www.hostinger.com/vps-hosting">VPS plan cards and prepaid note</a>. Calculations are labelled estimates.</p><h2>Prepaid billing and weekly backups</h2><p><strong>Hourly price: N/A for these prepaid term offers.</strong> Hostinger states <q>All plans are paid upfront.</q> [A]. The monthly display is a term-price equivalent, not a pay-by-the-hour rate.</p><p><strong>Weekly backups are included.</strong> The shared plan-features section explicitly says <q>Free weekly backups</q> [B]. This statement covers the included weekly feature; it does not establish a price or entitlement for daily backup add-ons.</p><h2>Cash-flow estimate: a renewal term is a whole prepaid purchase</h2><p><strong>S — analyst-defined scenario, not a Hostinger promise:</strong> observe the account over 36 months, keep the same plan, and complete one renewal for the same 24-month term shown on the card. Assume the quoted renewal rate remains applicable. Taxes and optional purchases are excluded. The 36-month observation horizon and the remaining 12 months used for allocation are our scenario choices.</p><p>Formula: cash paid after purchasing one renewal term = first payment + published renewal monthly equivalent × renewal-term months. A 36-month service-cost allocation instead uses only 12 months of that renewal. It is not the amount of cash needed to purchase the full renewal term. Renewal charge timing is not predicted here.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><tr><th scope="col">Plan</th><th scope="col">First payment, official</th><th scope="col">Renewal purchase, estimate</th><th scope="col">Cash paid including one renewal, estimate</th><th scope="col">36-month service allocation, estimate</th></tr><tr><td>KVM 1</td><td>$155.76 [H1]</td><td>$11.99 [H1] × 24 months [S] = <strong>$287.76, estimate</strong></td><td>$155.76 + $287.76 = <strong>$443.52, estimate</strong> [S]</td><td>$155.76 + $11.99 × 12 months [S] = <strong>$299.64, estimate</strong></td></tr><tr><td>KVM 2</td><td>$210.96 [H2]</td><td>$14.99 [H2] × 24 months [S] = <strong>$359.76, estimate</strong></td><td>$210.96 + $359.76 = <strong>$570.72, estimate</strong> [S]</td><td>$210.96 + $14.99 × 12 months [S] = <strong>$390.84, estimate</strong></td></tr><tr><td>KVM 4</td><td>$311.76 [H3]</td><td>$28.99 [H3] × 24 months [S] = <strong>$695.76, estimate</strong></td><td>$311.76 + $695.76 = <strong>$1007.52, estimate</strong> [S]</td><td>$311.76 + $28.99 × 12 months [S] = <strong>$659.64, estimate</strong></td></tr><tr><td>KVM 8</td><td>$623.76 [H4]</td><td>$49.99 [H4] × 24 months [S] = <strong>$1199.76, estimate</strong></td><td>$623.76 + $1199.76 = <strong>$1823.52, estimate</strong> [S]</td><td>$623.76 + $49.99 × 12 months [S] = <strong>$1223.64, estimate</strong></td></tr></table></div><p class="source-note">Data source: official Hostinger pages · 2026-11-12 12:05 UTC · <a href="https://www.hostinger.com/vps-hosting">VPS plan cards and prepaid note</a>. Calculations are labelled estimates.</p><p>Every row traces the first payment and renewal rate to its own H-labelled card below. Multipliers and totals are visible scenario calculations. This is a distinction between cash paid and service-cost allocation, not a discount comparison against an unverified regular price.</p><h2>Bandwidth limits and cancelling renewal</h2><p>When the monthly VPS allowance is exhausted, Hostinger documents throttling to <strong>10 Mbps</strong> for the rest of that month, with the allowance and speed restored at the next monthly reset [C, opening body paragraph and following explanation]. We do not turn that policy into an unverified per-GB fee.</p><p>To disable renewal, Hostinger directs users to Billing → Subscriptions → Manage → Cancel subscription. The service stays active until expiry. Disabling auto-renewal does not reverse or refund already processed payments [D, opening body paragraph and NOTES]. This is not a promise that cancelling refunds the unused portion of a prepaid term.</p><h2>Official evidence and retrieval time</h2><ol><li id="H1"><a href="https://www.hostinger.com/vps-hosting#pricing">H1: KVM 1 card</a>. Locate the price line, then the payment/renewal paragraph directly under Choose plan. <q>Today you pay $155.76 for 24 months.</q> Renewal-rate fragment: <q>$11.99/mo</q>. The paragraph gives the first-term length and states that renewal uses the same term.</li><li id="H2"><a href="https://www.hostinger.com/vps-hosting#pricing">H2: KVM 2 card</a>. Locate the price line, then the payment/renewal paragraph directly under Choose plan. Payment fragment: <q>$210.96</q>; renewal fragment: <q>$14.99/mo</q>. The paragraph gives the first-term length and states that renewal uses the same term.</li><li id="H3"><a href="https://www.hostinger.com/vps-hosting#pricing">H3: KVM 4 card</a>. Locate the price line, then the payment/renewal paragraph directly under Choose plan. Payment fragment: <q>$311.76</q>; renewal fragment: <q>$28.99/mo</q>. The paragraph gives the first-term length and states that renewal uses the same term.</li><li id="H4"><a href="https://www.hostinger.com/vps-hosting#pricing">H4: KVM 8 card</a>. Locate the price line, then the payment/renewal paragraph directly under Choose plan. Payment fragment: <q>$623.76</q>; renewal fragment: <q>$49.99/mo</q>. The paragraph gives the first-term length and states that renewal uses the same term.</li></ol><ul><li id="R1">R1: KVM 1, official VPS purchase flow; Period = 1 month. Renewal sentence fragment: <q>Renews after 1 month at $19.49/mo</q>. The displayed crossed-out amount is the same. Source: <a href="https://www.hostinger.com/vps-hosting#pricing">official VPS page → Choose plan → Period</a>.</li><li id="R2">R2: KVM 2, official VPS purchase flow; Period = 1 month. Renewal sentence fragment: <q>Renews after 1 month at $24.49/mo</q>. The displayed crossed-out amount is the same. Source: <a href="https://www.hostinger.com/vps-hosting#pricing">official VPS page → Choose plan → Period</a>.</li><li id="R3">R3: KVM 4, official VPS purchase flow; Period = 1 month. Renewal sentence fragment: <q>Renews after 1 month at $42.99/mo</q>. The displayed crossed-out amount is the same. Source: <a href="https://www.hostinger.com/vps-hosting#pricing">official VPS page → Choose plan → Period</a>.</li><li id="R4">R4: KVM 8, official VPS purchase flow; Period = 1 month. Renewal sentence fragment: <q>Renews after 1 month at $73.99/mo</q>. The displayed crossed-out amount is the same. Source: <a href="https://www.hostinger.com/vps-hosting#pricing">official VPS page → Choose plan → Period</a>.</li><li><a href="https://www.hostinger.com/vps-hosting">A: VPS page, note below the shared features list</a>: prepayment and monthly-equivalent explanation; footer: amounts exclude VAT.</li><li><a href="https://www.hostinger.com/vps-hosting">B: VPS page, shared plan features</a>: included weekly-backup label.</li><li><a href="https://www.hostinger.com/support/8789965-what-happens-if-your-vps-bandwidth-resource-limits-are-exceeded/">C: bandwidth-limit help article</a>: opening body paragraph and explanation before Monitoring bandwidth usage.</li><li><a href="https://www.hostinger.com/support/1583234-how-to-disable-auto-renewal-at-hostinger/">D: disabling auto-renewal help article</a>: opening body paragraph, dashboard instructions and NOTES.</li></ul><p>Price-card retrieval: <strong>2026-11-12 12:05 UTC</strong>. Promotions and renewal offers may change; final checkout, eligibility and applicable taxes require confirmation. No promotional end date, daily-backup surcharge or per-GB overage rate is asserted here.</p><p><a href="./sources.json">Download the timestamped numerical evidence</a></p></main><footer>VPS Cost Lens · Independent price research</footer></body></html>'
